{
  "schema": "ppp.bench-correctness/1",
  "written_by": "independent fixture author (spec-derived, no reader consulted)",
  "conventions": "All positions and durations are in quarter notes, written as exact fraction strings (\"0\", \"1/2\", \"3/2\", \"6\"): a note's length is <duration> divided by the <divisions> in force at that point. onset_q counts from the start of the first measure in the file (0). A measure's len_q is its content length (the furthest point the <duration>/<backup>/<forward> cursor reaches), so an implicit pickup measure is only as long as what it contains. \"sounding\" lists key presses: two notes are joined into one entry (dur_q = the sum) only when one carries <tie type=\"start\"/> and the next note of the same pitch carries <tie type=\"stop\"/> and starts exactly when the first ends; a <tied>-only connection, or a tie start with no matching tie stop, does not join. Chord notes are separate entries with the same onset; rests are not listed; grace notes take no time, are not listed, and are counted in grace_notes. midi = (octave + 1) * 12 + step semitone (C0 D2 E4 F5 G7 A9 B11) + alter, taken from <pitch> exactly as written, because MusicXML pitch data is the sounding pitch: the key signature, <accidental> and <octave-shift> never change it. step and alter are as written in <pitch> (alter 0 when absent); staff is the note's <staff> value (1 when absent). Entries are sorted by (onset_q, staff, midi). time is the first <time> as [beats, beat-type]; key is the first <key>, with mode null when it has no <mode>. tempo.sound_qpm is the first <sound tempo> value (already quarter notes per minute); tempo.printed_qpm is the first <metronome> converted to quarter notes per minute (per-minute times the beat-unit length in quarters, dots included); tempo.marks_qpm lists every <metronome> and every <sound tempo> in document order, both converted to quarter notes per minute (within one <direction> the metronome in <direction-type> comes before its <sound>); null or [] when there are none.",
